---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---
<BaseLayout title="Copyright and Takedown Policy" description="Read WasmStore's copyright and takedown process, including the information rights holders should provide when requesting review of a listing or external link." path="/copyright">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">PIXEL ARCADE · RIGHTS & RESPONSIBILITY</div><h1>COPYRIGHT &amp; <span class="gradient-text">TAKEDOWNS</span></h1><p>A clear, practical route for rights holders and authorized representatives to raise an intellectual-property concern.</p></div></section>
  <article class="prose wrap legal-page">
    <p class="legal-kicker">RIGHTS REVIEW / NOTICE PROCESS</p>
    <p>WasmStore is an independent discovery directory. Pages may describe third-party games and link to external demos, repositories, or project websites. A listing is not a statement that WasmStore owns, hosts, endorses, or has permission to redistribute the underlying game or its assets. External websites are operated by their respective owners.</p>
    <p>Some entries refer to community-made browser ports or code published in public repositories, including projects found on GitHub. Where a project is open source, its own license governs that project's code and permitted uses; public availability alone does not make every game asset or trademark open source. WasmStore does not claim to own or hold licenses for proprietary games such as Grand Theft Auto titles or Minecraft, and a third-party port's license does not automatically grant rights to the original game's name, artwork, audio, or other protected material. Listings are provided for discovery and attribution, and may link to the project or provider rather than represent an authorized distribution.</p>
    <h2>1. When to contact us</h2><p>Please contact us if you believe a WasmStore page contains inaccurate attribution, uses material in a way that raises a copyright or trademark concern, links to material that should be reviewed, or otherwise misrepresents your work. If the material is hosted on another service, you may also need to contact that host directly.</p>
    <h2>2. Information to include in a notice</h2><p>To help us identify the issue, include as much of the following as applies:</p><ul><li>Your full name and a reliable email address.</li><li>The rights holder's name and your authority to act for them, if you are a representative.</li><li>The exact WasmStore page URL and a clear description of the material in question.</li><li>A description of the protected work, mark, or other right involved.</li><li>A URL to an authorized source or to the material you want reviewed, where available.</li><li>An explanation of why you believe the listing or link is problematic and what action you are requesting.</li><li>A good-faith statement that the information you provide is accurate and that you are the rights holder or authorized to act on their behalf.</li></ul>
    <h2>3. How to submit</h2><p>Visit the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>, choose “Copyright / takedown request,” and include the details above. You may also email <a href={'mailto:'+site.contactEmail}>{site.contactEmail}</a>. Use “Copyright / Takedown Request” in the subject line so the purpose is easy to identify.</p>
    <h2>4. Review and possible actions</h2><p>We review notices based on the information supplied and may ask for clarification. Depending on the circumstances, we may correct attribution, update or remove a directory entry, disable a link, or take no action if the concern is unclear or unsupported. We aim to handle reports thoughtfully, but we do not guarantee a specific outcome or response time.</p>
    <h2>5. Third-party hosting</h2><p>WasmStore may not host the material referenced by a listing. Removing a link from this directory does not remove content from the third-party service that operates it. If you need content removed from an external host, contact that provider and follow its own formal notice process.</p>
    <h2>6. Counter-notices and disputed reports</h2><p>If you are the project maintainer and believe a listing was reported in error, contact us with the affected URL, relevant license or authorization information, and a concise explanation. We will consider the information available. This contact channel is not a substitute for any formal legal procedure required by applicable law.</p>
    <h2>7. Good-faith use of this process</h2><p>Please provide accurate information and report only material you are entitled to raise concerns about. Do not include passwords, financial account details, or unrelated sensitive information. False or incomplete reports may delay review.</p>
    <h2>8. Important limitation</h2><p>This page provides general information about the directory's review process and is not legal advice. It does not establish that WasmStore qualifies as a designated agent under any particular law or jurisdiction. If a formal statutory notice is required, consult the applicable law and submit the notice through the legally appropriate channel.</p>
    <p>For the ownership and independence context, also see the <a href="/non-affiliation">Non-Affiliation Notice</a> and <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
  </article>
  <style>.legal-page{max-width:900px;padding-top:12px;padding-bottom:64px;line-height:1.8}.legal-page .legal-kicker{font:700 11px/1.5 var(--font-pixel);letter-spacing:.08em;color:#6b55d8}.legal-page h2{font-family:var(--font-pixel);font-size:clamp(18px,2vw,24px);line-height:1.4;margin-top:34px;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink);text-transform:uppercase}.legal-page p,.legal-page li{font-size:16px}.legal-page a{color:#5b43c6;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:3px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.legal-page a:hover{color:#d73569}@media(max-width:600px){.legal-page{padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px}.legal-page p,.legal-page li{font-size:15px}.legal-page h2{font-size:17px}}</style>
</BaseLayout>